# Genesis Provider Usage — {{ model.names.namespace }}

Genesis providers abstract AWS infrastructure so vertical services stay portable and testable. This service has the following modules wired:

{{ for module in model.selected_modules }}
- **{{ module.name }}** → `{{ module.package_name }}`
{{ end }}

---

## Registration Pattern

All Genesis modules are registered in `Program.cs` — **never** register them again in vertical code:

```csharp
// Already in Program.cs — do not duplicate
{{ for module in model.selected_modules }}
builder.Services.{{ module.di_extension_name }}(builder.Configuration.GetSection("{{ module.name }}"));
{{ end }}
```

## Injection Pattern

Inject Genesis interfaces at the **service layer only** — never in `ServiceImpl` or `Program.cs`:

```csharp
public sealed class YourDomainService : IYourDomainService
{
    private readonly ICache _cache;               // Genesis.Caching
    private readonly IFileStorage _fileStorage;   // Genesis.FileStorage
    private readonly IWorkflow _workflow;         // Genesis.Workflow

    public YourDomainService(ICache cache, IFileStorage fileStorage, IWorkflow workflow)
    {
        _cache       = cache;
        _fileStorage = fileStorage;
        _workflow    = workflow;
    }
}
```

---

## Caching (Genesis.Caching.AWS)

```csharp
// Get with null return on miss
var record = await _cache.GetAsync<YourDomainRecord>($"{{ model.names.cache_prefix }}{id}", ct)
    .ConfigureAwait(false);

// Set with TTL
await _cache.SetAsync($"{{ model.names.cache_prefix }}{id}", record, TimeSpan.FromMinutes(5), ct)
    .ConfigureAwait(false);

// Delete on mutation
await _cache.RemoveAsync($"{{ model.names.cache_prefix }}{id}", ct).ConfigureAwait(false);
```

**Cache key convention:** `{{ model.names.cache_prefix }}{entity-type}:{id}` — always use the interpolated prefix, never a string literal.

**TTL guidance:**
- Read-heavy reference data → 5–30 minutes
- User-facing frequently-changing data → 30–60 seconds
- Always invalidate on write

---

## File Storage (Genesis.FileStorage.AWS)

```csharp
// Upload
var key = $"{{ model.names.namespace | string.downcase }}/{id}/document.pdf";
await _fileStorage.UploadAsync(key, stream, contentType: "application/pdf", ct)
    .ConfigureAwait(false);

// Generate a pre-signed download URL (valid for 15 minutes)
var url = await _fileStorage.GetPresignedUrlAsync(key, TimeSpan.FromMinutes(15), ct)
    .ConfigureAwait(false);

// Delete
await _fileStorage.DeleteAsync(key, ct).ConfigureAwait(false);
```

---

## Workflow (Genesis.Workflow.AWS)

```csharp
// Start a Step Functions workflow execution
var executionArn = await _workflow.StartExecutionAsync(
    stateMachineArn: configuration["Workflow:StateMachineArn"],
    input: new { RecordId = id, Action = "process" },
    ct).ConfigureAwait(false);

// Check status
var status = await _workflow.GetExecutionStatusAsync(executionArn, ct).ConfigureAwait(false);
```

---

## Testing with Genesis Mocks

In `TestBase.ConfigureTestServices`, replace Genesis providers with mocks to avoid AWS calls in tests:

```csharp
protected override void ConfigureTestServices(IServiceCollection services)
{
    var cacheMock = new Mock<ICache>();
    cacheMock.Setup(c => c.GetAsync<YourDomainRecord>(It.IsAny<string>(), default))
             .ReturnsAsync((YourDomainRecord?)null);

    services.AddSingleton(cacheMock.Object);
    // Repeat for IFileStorage, IWorkflow as needed
}
```
